{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the result.\n\n## Area object decoder: **CPU $950A** (prgRom 0x150A)\n\n**How I found it**\n- Got into World 1-1, then ran `trace_writes` in **read** mode over 1‑1's layout data (CPU $A68E–$A78D; `$E7/$E8` = $A690, set by `LoadAreaData` at $9C22) while the attract demo loaded 1‑1.\n- The reads came from PCs inside one routine: **$9516** (`LDA ($E7),Y` → `CMP #$FD`), $9522, $9533, plus the object spawner's $95A1/$95E9/$95F3/$9600/$962A/$964B.\n- Disassembling backwards from $9516 past the loop head gave the first instruction **$950A** (`STX $08 / LDA #$00 / STA $0729 / LDY $072C / LDA ($E7),Y`), preceded by the RTS at $9503 and 6 data bytes. Like other SMB routines it has no direct JSR/JMP, so it's reached by the game's indirect dispatch.\n\n**How it reads the records**\n- Y = `$072C`, the byte offset into the layout stream (`$E7/$E8`); `$FD` ends the data. It reads the record's second byte, whose **bit 7 is a page-break flag** (page counter `$072A/$072B`); the first byte's low nibble is the object type (special $0D/$0E handled specially). Objects are built only when the record's page reaches the target page `$0725` (via the spawner at $9595); otherwise the offset is advanced by `$9589` (INC $072C twice).\n\n**Proof (throwaway hack `eval-sheet4-b`, all undone)**\n- Ledgered `write_memory prgRom 0x2695` — the x byte of layout record `[57 00]` — from `0x00` to `0x1F`, then `reset_emulator` + `reapply_edits` and re‑entered 1‑1.\n- At the **same camera** (TIME 390, identical hill and two ? blocks on the left), the untouched run shows the normal right-side brick/?-block row; with the edit the decoder builds a **totally different structure** there (a tall green-capped pipe/wall column). A control `$FD` over the first layout byte (0x2690) removed the interactive pipes/? blocks entirely.\n- `undo_edit` restored 0x00 (ledger now empty).\n\n**Recorded / finalized**\n- `record_mapping` routine **0x950A**, name **\"area object decoder\"** (confidence 1), with the trace + disassembly + write proof in the notes.\n- `promote_mappings` saved it (mappings file now includes the routine).\n- `use_hack default` — the emulator is back on the default (empty) hack, ROM clean."}
